<Base
  title="Research"
  description="Research by Dr Kalonji A. Tshisekedi — population genomics, multi-omics integration, and health data science for precision medicine in underrepresented populations."
>
  <div class="section" style="padding-top: 4vw;">
    <div class="section-narrow">
      <h1>Research</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">Understanding human genetic diversity to make precision medicine genuinely precise for everyone.</p>

      <p>
        The way we study human genetics today is <strong>fundamentally skewed</strong>. The vast majority of genomic research draws from populations of European descent — leaving the most genetically diverse continent, Africa, as the least represented in the data that drives drug development, diagnostic tools, and treatment decisions.
      </p>
      <p>
        My research is about <strong>changing that equation</strong>. I combine population genomics, multi-omics approaches, and data science to produce insights that are more representative, more inclusive, and ultimately more useful for human health.
      </p>

      <div class="research-area">
        <h2>Population Genomics & African Genetic Diversity</h2>
        <p>
          African populations harbour more genetic diversity than the rest of the world combined — yet they remain vastly underrepresented in global genomic studies. My work focuses on <strong>characterising genetic variation in understudied African communities</strong>, developing computational frameworks for population-scale sequencing data, and contributing to the growing body of knowledge that will make precision medicine genuinely precise for everyone.
        </p>
        <p>
          This includes variant calling and annotation pipelines for whole-genome and whole-exome data, population structure analysis, and pharmacogenomics studies that connect genetic variants to drug response.
        </p>
        <div class="research-tags">
          <span class="research-tag">WGS / WES</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Population structure</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Pharmacogenomics</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Human genetics</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="research-area">
        <h2>Multi-Omics Integration</h2>
        <p>
          A genome sequence tells you what's possible. But understanding what's actually happening in a biological system requires looking at multiple layers simultaneously — DNA, RNA, proteins, metabolites. I integrate data across <strong>genomics, proteomics, and metagenomics</strong> to build richer, more complete biological models.
        </p>
        <p>
          My training spans both wet-lab techniques (NGS library prep, LC-MS/MS sample processing) and the computational side (bioinformatics pipelines, statistical modelling, and multi-omics data integration frameworks). This dual fluency lets me design studies end-to-end, from sample collection to insight.
        </p>
        <div class="research-tags">
          <span class="research-tag">NGS</span>
          <span class="research-tag">LC-MS/MS</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Metagenomics</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Proteomics</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Multi-omics</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="research-area">
        <h2>Health Data Science & Translational Research</h2>
        <p>
          Biological datasets are growing faster than our ability to make sense of them. I develop <strong>computational pipelines and machine learning approaches</strong> to extract meaningful patterns from large-scale genomic and health data — with a focus on translational applications that connect bench science to clinical relevance.
        </p>
        <p>
          Whether it's building variant annotation tools, applying unsupervised learning to population-scale datasets, or creating reproducible analysis workflows, the goal is always the same: turn data into decisions that improve outcomes.
        </p>
        <div class="research-tags">
          <span class="research-tag">Machine learning</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Pipelines</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Python / R</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Reproducibility</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Cloud computing</span>
        </div>
      </div>

